.TH GNOME-VOICE-SERVER 1 "October 2026" "gnome-voice-server 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gnome-voice-server \- store and serve GNOME Voice voicegrams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gnome-voice-server
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gnome-voice-server
accepts voicegrams \(em Ogg Vorbis recordings and their Voicegram XML
(\fI.voice\fR) metadata \(em uploaded over HTTP by the
.BR gnome-voice (1)
client or
.BR gnome-voice-send (1),
stores them on disk, and serves them back for listing and playback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Read settings from the [server] group of \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address =\fIADDR\fR
Listen on \fIADDR\fR only. Default: all interfaces.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
TCP port. Default 8085; 0 picks a free port.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-storage\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Directory holding the voicegrams.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-public\-url =\fIURL\fR
Base URL written into \fI<stream>\fR links, e.g. https://voice.example.org.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-token\-file =\fIFILE\fR
Require \fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR with the token in \fIFILE\fR for
uploads, and enable deletion.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-size =\fIBYTES\fR
Largest accepted recording. Default 32 MiB.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-clients =\fIN\fR
Concurrent connections. Default 32.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-read\-only
Serve stored voicegrams but refuse uploads.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GVS_TOKEN
Upload token, used when no token file is configured.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/gnome-voice-server/gnome-voice-server.conf
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/gnome-voice-server/voicegrams/
Stored \fIID\fR.ogg and \fIID\fR.voice files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-voice-send (1),
.BR gnome-voice (1)
.PP
The wire protocol is described in PROTOCOL.md in the source distribution.
